---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PORTAL, TRIAL } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Self-hosted patch and estate management"
  description="ServerPerch is a self-hosted virtual appliance for update management, monitoring and inventory across your Linux and Windows estate. Your servers, your data, your keys."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Patch and estate management that stays on your network</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        ServerPerch is a self-hosted virtual appliance for update management, monitoring
        and inventory across your Linux and Windows machines. No SaaS control plane, no
        data leaves your estate — you run it, you own it.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={PORTAL.signup}>
          Start a {TRIAL.days}-day trial
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/pricing">See pricing</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What ServerPerch does</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        One appliance, one console: the operational view of your estate that normally
        takes three tools and a spreadsheet.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Update management</h3>
          <p>
            See pending OS and package updates across Debian, Ubuntu and RHEL-family
            machines, group them by policy, and roll them out on your schedule — with
            per-machine outcomes recorded.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Monitoring and inventory</h3>
          <p>
            A lightweight agent reports machine health, installed packages and update
            status. Live dashboards, a NOC wallboard view, and alerting on the things
            that actually break.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Remote operations</h3>
          <p>
            Push-install agents over SSH or WinRM, run signed jobs against tagged
            machine groups, and open audited terminal sessions — all through the same
            appliance.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h2>On-prem by design</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        ServerPerch ships as a virtual appliance (OVA, VHDX or qcow2) that you deploy on
        your own hypervisor. It is built for estates where the patch server itself has
        to be trustworthy.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>No outbound dependency</h3>
          <p>
            A running appliance does not need internet access to keep working. Licences
            are signed documents verified offline, and agents keep checking in even if
            the licence check-in is overdue. Air-gapped installs are supported with
            offline licence files and update bundles.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Your keys, your data</h3>
          <p>
            Agents authenticate over mutually authenticated TLS to your appliance, not
            to us. Inventory, recordings and update history stay in your database, on
            your hardware.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h2>How a rollout looks</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>1. Deploy</h3>
          <p>
            Import the appliance image, answer the first-boot questions, and enrol your
            first machines with a one-line install command or push-install.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>2. Activate</h3>
          <p>
            Enter your licence key from the customer portal — or import an offline
            licence file if the appliance can't reach the internet.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>3. Manage</h3>
          <p>
            Set update policies per machine group, watch results come in, and let the
            daily licence check-in renew itself in the background.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="cta-band">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Try it on your own estate</h2>
      <p>
        The trial gives you {TRIAL.days} days and {TRIAL.machines} managed machines —
        no card required. Sign-up takes a minute and issues your licence key
        immediately.
      </p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={PORTAL.signup}>Create a trial account</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
